Recommends: sg3-utils, psmisc, lsscsi
Description: Synology NAS storage plugin for Proxmox VE
 A Proxmox VE custom storage plugin for Synology NAS over iSCSI, in which one
 VM disk is one thin LUN on the NAS, so DSM's own snapshots and clones act on
 the unit an operator thinks about — no LVM layer and no shared LUN carved up
 locally.
 .
 Registers the storage type "synologysan". Allocation, activation, snapshots,
 rollback, clones, resize, export/import and live migration have been verified
 against real hardware, and a rollback has been checked at the block level.
 .
 Every 0.x release is a prerelease. Synology publishes no specification for the
 SAN Manager Web API, so everything array-facing was established by reading
 Synology's own CSI driver against OpenStack Cinder's and then measuring a real
 NAS. See /usr/share/doc/jt-pve-storage-synology/TESTING.md for exactly what has
 been verified and what has not.
 .
 Also ships pve-syno-api-probe, a read-only tool that asks a DSM what it
 supports. It creates nothing and deletes nothing, and is safe against a
 production NAS.
 .
 The plugin must be installed on every node of the cluster.
